    {
      "id": "the-tempest/sceneIII_32.1/p@76517",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MIRANDA.\nAt mine unworthiness, that dare not offer\nWhat I desire to give; and much less take\nWhat I shall die to want. But this is trifling;\nAnd all the more it seeks to hide itself,\nThe bigger bulk it shows. Hence, bashful cunning!\nAnd prompt me, plain and holy innocence!\nI am your wife if you will marry me;\nIf not, I’ll die your maid: to be your fellow\nYou may deny me; but I’ll be your servant,\nWhether you will or no.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-tempest/sceneIII_32.1/p@76517/line-1",
